<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR rises to 13.21 from 13.11 percent.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR rises to 13.21 from 13.11 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) for one month rose to 13.21 from 13.11 percent and the bid rate (Athibid) firmed to 12.74 from 12.63 percent.</p>
<p>ATHIBOR</p>
<p> DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH   12-MTH</p>
<p> Sept 09  13.21   13.22   13.24   13.32   13.42   13.62</p>
<p> Sept 06  13.11   13.15   13.19   13.29   13.43   13.61</p>
<p> Sept 05  12.95   13.02   13.07   13.23   13.41   13.59</p>
<p> Sept 04  12.99   13.08   13.11   13.24   13.43   13.60</p>
<p> Sept 03  13.01   13.08   13.13   13.25   13.46   13.62</p>
<p> Sept 02  12.96   13.02   13.05   13.22   13.41   13.62</p>
<p> Aug  30  12.87   12.93   12.98   13.17   13.41   13.57</p>
<p> Aug  29  13.08   13.14   13.22   13.41   13.66   13.82</p>
<p>ATHIBID</p>
<p> Sept 09  12.74   12.76   12.78   12.83   12.91   13.09</p>
<p> Sept 06  12.63   12.68   12.72   12.80   12.92   13.09</p>
<p> Sept 05  12.47   12.54   12.59   12.76   12.90   13.06</p>
<p> Sept 04  12.51   12.60   12.63   12.77   12.93   13.09</p>
<p> Sept 03  12.53   12.60   12.64   12.76   12.93   13.10</p>
<p> Sept 02  12.47   12.53   12.57   12.73   12.91   13.10</p>
<p> Aug  30  12.40   12.46   12.50   12.67   12.90   13.04</p>
<p> Aug  29  12.59   12.66   12.72   12.92   13.16   13.30</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 13 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
